    {
      "id": "9-production-2080",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1380.1,
      "y": 12367,
      "width": 636.48,
      "height": 180,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2843285228,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1266023277,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794883834837,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "section": "9-production",
        "anchor": [
          1380.1,
          12367,
          "lt"
        ]
      },
      "text": "the library's prefill takes fresh K and V packed\nflat with cumulative lengths, no block table; it is\nCUDA for B200-class GPUs only. the older kernel\nreads each block where it lies, through the table;\nours gathers K and V into a copy at every layer.\nnone of this code runs on the Mac",
      "originalText": "the library's prefill takes fresh K and V packed\nflat with cumulative lengths, no block table; it is\nCUDA for B200-class GPUs only. the older kernel\nreads each block where it lies, through the table;\nours gathers K and V into a copy at every layer.\nnone of this code runs on the Mac",
      "fontSize": 24,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "bWY"
    },
    {
      "id": "9-production-2081",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 12637,
      "width": 1794,
      "height": 112.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2425362608,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1267432931,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794883834837,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "section": "9-production",
        "anchor": [
          0,
          12637,
          "lt"
        ]
      },
      "text": "At startup it pops its first free block and makes that the null block; freed blocks with no cached prefix go to the\nfront of its free queue. Its kernel takes the physical block from the table, rebuilds a position as block × size\n+ offset, and finds a query head's KV head by division. Ours gathers a copy where that kernel reads in place.",
      "originalText": "At startup it pops its first free block and makes that the null block; freed blocks with no cached prefix go to the\nfront of its free queue. Its kernel takes the physical block from the table, rebuilds a position as block × size\n+ offset, and finds a query head's KV head by division. Ours gathers a copy where that kernel reads in place.",
      "fontSize": 30,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "bWZ"
    },
